      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "We first simplify the function using the identity $\\arctan a + \\arctan b = \\arctan \\left( \\frac{a + b}{1 - ab} \\right)$.\nUsing this identity, we have\n\\[f(x) = \\arctan x + \\arctan \\frac{1 - x}{1 + x} = \\arctan x + \\arctan \\left( \\frac{(1 - x) + x}{(1 - x)(1 + x)} \\right) = \\arctan x + \\arctan 0.\\]\nSince $\\arctan 0 = 0$, we have $f(x) = \\arctan x + 0 = \\arctan x.$\nSince the function $\\arctan x$ takes on all values between $-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, the function $f(x)$ also takes on all values between $-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.\nTherefore, the numbers in the range of $f(x)$ are $\\boxed{-\\frac{\\pi}{2}, -\\frac{\\pi}{4}, 0, \\frac{\\pi}{4}, \\frac{\\pi}{2}}.$. The answer is: -\\frac{\\pi}{2},-\\frac{\\pi}{4},0,\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{\\pi}{2}",
